            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0881" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.6363 African Exploration and Development
                    Corp./9: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-08-31T16:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1935—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>236. Your 418, August 31, noon.<anchor n="94" xml:id="d647-f1"/> In reply to
                    questions raised at the press conference this morning I stressed the fact that
                    we knew nothing about the African Exploration and Development Corporation <pb
                        facs="0882" n="780" xml:id="pg780"/> or its plans and that we had no advance
                    information that the corporation was seeking a concession in Ethiopia. I added
                    that on the basis of facts now available I could not see that any question
                    presented itself to this Government.</p>
                <p>You should inform the Foreign Office in the above sense and keep the Department
                    fully and promptly informed of any developments that may come to the attention
                    of the British authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
